Write a semgrep rule for this. Our ingestion workers at example.com parse customer-supplied config bundles, and I found this in the ml-ingest repo:

```python
import yaml

def load_bundle(path):
    with open(path) as f:
        return yaml.load(f.read())

def load_bundle_loader(path):
    with open(path) as f:
        return yaml.load(f, Loader=yaml.Loader)
```

yaml.load without a safe loader can construct arbitrary Python objects, so an uploaded bundle can run code. I want the rule to flag unsafe use but not yaml.safe_load or yaml.load with SafeLoader.
